// Issue #362: an erase plus an insert in one for-in body restores the net
// size, so a size check misses it and the loop ends silently. The
// structural version check must fail on every backend instead, with empty
// stdout. The insert key derives from the loop variable: a plain use in
// m.del(k) alone does not satisfy the tooling resolver's unused-local pass
// (see issue #387). An error_probes entry in tools/check_jvm_probes.sh and
// tools/check_clr_probes.sh.
var m = {1: "a"};
for (var k in m) {
    m.del(k);
    m[k + 100] = "b";
}
